{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-6476",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The Law of Sines states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡B}{b}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡A}{a}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\nb=9,\\,m∠A={25}^{∘},\\,a=8\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡B}{9} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{8} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡B & =9\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{8} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{9\\cdot 0.422\\,62}{8} \\\\  & ≈0.475\\,45,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠B & ≈\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.475\\,45)≈{28.39}^{∘},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places. But this is less than ${90}^{∘}.$ To get the true value of $B,$ we subtract our answer from ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\nm∠B≈{180}^{∘}-{28.39}^{∘}≈{151.61}^{∘}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
